-- title:
--   Transversality of the two branches in the stalk over A
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of level $\{p\}$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with a compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K$, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and write $X =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) with structure morphism $f =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ and $X_k$ for the pullback of $f$ along $\mathrm{Spec}\,k \to \mathrm{Spec}\,A$. Assume given two proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$, geometrically integral schemes $c_1 : C_1 \to \mathrm{Spec}\,k$ and $c_2 : C_2 \to \mathrm{Spec}\,k$, both with integral underlying scheme, and closed immersions $i_1 : C_1 \to X_k$, $i_2 : C_2 \to X_k$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,k$ (the structure morphism of $X_k$ being the second projection), whose images jointly cover the points of $X_k$; assume the scheme-theoretic intersection $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2$ is reduced, its set of points has cardinality $n > 0$, and let $\nu$ be one of its points. Let $x \in X$ be the image of $\nu$ under $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2 \to C_1 \to X_k \to X$, and assume hypotheses $h_1$, $h_2$ stating that the images $\xi_1, \xi_2 \in X$ of the generic points of $C_1$, $C_2$ under $i_1$, $i_2$ followed by $X_k \to X$ both specialise to $x$. The conclusion is that the two branch ideals $\mathrm{Scheme.branchIdeal}\,h_i \subseteq \mathcal{O}_{X,x}$, each the preimage of the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,\xi_i}$ under the specialisation map $\mathcal{O}_{X,x} \to \mathcal{O}_{X,\xi_i}$, satisfy $\mathrm{branchIdeal}\,h_1 + \mathrm{branchIdeal}\,h_2 = \mathfrak{m}_x$.
--
--   This is the transversality statement at a crossing point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$: the two ideals cutting out the branches through $x$ generate the whole maximal ideal of the local ring of the model at $x$. It is used in the construction of oriented étale crossing charts at such points and in the identification of the branch ideals with vanishing ideals of the corresponding integral subschemes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_branchIdeal_sup_branchIdeal_eq_maximalIdeal_stalk_of_isReduced_pullback_twoChartModel_x1_mul.lean

